      "id": "wjc6wbq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Definition of Computer"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Computers perform four core operations: receiving input, processing data, producing output, and storing results.",
        "Computers are classified based on operation into Analog (continuous physical data), Digital (discrete binary data), and Hybrid (combined features).",
        "Computer evolution spans five generations, progressing from Vacuum Tubes to Transistors, Integrated Circuits, Microprocessors, and Artificial Intelligence.",
        "Primary characteristics of a computer include high processing speed, extreme accuracy, high diligence, versatility, and vast storage capacity."
      ],
      "id": "1ftka80"
    },
