    {
      "id": "6sgbyip",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.4 Generations of Computers"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "First-generation computers used Vacuum Tubes, second-generation used Transistors, third-generation used Integrated Circuits (ICs), fourth-generation used VLSI/Microprocessors, and fifth-generation rely on ULSI/AI.",
        "Hybrid computers combine the continuous measurement of Analog computers with the precise logical counting of Digital computers (frequently cited example: ECG machines in medical units).",
        "Questions frequently test the distinction between data processing stages: Input -> Processing -> Output -> Storage (IPOS cycle)."
      ],
      "id": "kmu6ipl"
    },
